<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="QueryFlag: Support" id="QueryFlag-Reference-and-Support">

  <primary-label ref="queryflag"/>

  <tldr>
    <p>Issues: <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/dorkag/issues">edgafner/dorkag on GitHub</a></p>
    <p>E-mail: <a href="mailto:jgafner@dorkag.com">jgafner@dorkag.com</a></p>
  </tldr>

  <link-summary>Report a QueryFlag bug, request a feature, contact the developer, or read the release notes.</link-summary>
  <card-summary>Report a bug, request a feature, contact the developer, or read the release notes.</card-summary>
  <web-summary>Get support for the QueryFlag plugin for JetBrains IDEs: report bugs, request features on GitHub, contact the developer, and read the release notes.</web-summary>

  <p>
    Before you report a problem, check <a href="QueryFlag-Troubleshooting.topic"/>.
  </p>

  <chapter title="Report a bug or request a feature" id="feature_request_and_bug">
    <p>
      Report QueryFlag issues in the public <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/dorkag/issues">edgafner/dorkag</a> repository on GitHub.
      Use the QueryFlag issue templates and include your IDE version, QueryFlag version, database type, and the steps to reproduce the problem.
    </p>
    <list>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/dorkag/issues/new?template=bug_queryflag_report.md">Report a QueryFlag bug</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/dorkag/issues/new?template=feature_queryflag_request.md">Request a QueryFlag feature</a>
      </li>
    </list>
    <p>
      If the IDE shows a QueryFlag error, click <control>Report Exception</control> in the IDE error dialog.
      It opens a new QueryFlag bug report on GitHub.
      Copy the stack trace from the error dialog into the report, together with your IDE and QueryFlag versions.
    </p>
    <note>
      Issues on GitHub are public.
      Remove passwords, host names, and data from queries before you submit a report.
    </note>
  </chapter>

  <chapter title="Contact the developer" id="contact_me">
    <p>
      For licensing questions or anything you do not want to post publicly, e-mail
      <a href="mailto:jgafner@dorkag.com">jgafner@dorkag.com</a>.
    </p>
  </chapter>

  <chapter title="Data and privacy" id="privacy">
    <p>
      QueryFlag sends no usage statistics and does not connect to any server itself.
      It runs your queries through the data sources of the <control>Database</control> tool window.
      For what a template stores, see <a href="QueryFlag-Settings.topic" anchor="storage">Where QueryFlag stores settings</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="privacy-policy.topic">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </chapter>
  <chapter title="Release notes" id="release-notes">
    <p>
      The <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/18269-queryflag/versions">Versions</a> page on JetBrains Marketplace
      lists every QueryFlag release with its change notes and compatible IDE versions.
    </p>
  </chapter>

